WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.640
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.320
Today, the awesome power of antioxidants.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.680
And we start with an investigation
into which bean, berry, and lentil

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.120
has the highest antioxidant power.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.680
An apple a day has been
associated with as much as

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.960
a 35 percent lower risk
of premature death,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.360
but which apple is best?

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.840
Whichever apple
you'll eat the most.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.600
So, eat your favorite apple.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.360
But if you don't care
which apple you eat,

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.480
or you're just curious,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.080
which apple has the highest
antioxidant content:

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.240
Fuji, Gala, Golden Delicious,
Granny Smith, Pink Lady,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.840
or Red Delicious?

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.200
For apples,
Granny gets the gold,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.280
with more than
twice as many antioxidants

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.000
than Golden Delicious apples.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.040
Interestingly, antioxidant
content roughly corresponds

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.040
with the ability
to lower cholesterol levels

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:05.920
within one month

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.640
for those randomized to eat
an apple a day.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.160
Annurca apples beat
Granny Smith, but presumably,

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.960
it's because study participants
got two Annurcas a day

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.160
versus just one of the others,

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.480
because they were
about half the size.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.280
But two apples
even when they're half the size,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.080
have more overall surface area,

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.560
and the magic
may be in the peel.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.160
If you randomize people to eat
apples with or without the peel,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.320
you see a significant boost
in artery function

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.880
within an hour
of peel consumption.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:38.320
So, don't peel your apples.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.520
For other foods, the antioxidant
spread can be even greater.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.049
Check out nuts.

00:01:43.176 --> 00:01:44.960
Walnuts for the win!

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.360
Followed by pecans,
then pistachios,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.280
and who would have guessed
almonds would be

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.360
way down here at the bottom?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.920
Walnuts also have
the highest omega-3 content,

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.320
by a large margin,
beat out other nuts

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.160
in suppressing the growth
of cancer cells

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.440
in a Petri dish.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.360
And walnuts are
the only nuts shown

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.360
to markedly improve
human artery function.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.520
Blackberries
beat out blueberries

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.600
for antioxidant capacity.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.360
The beans surprised me.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.520
What do you think fits the bill
for best bean,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.440
at least
from an antioxidant perspective?

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.160
Want to pause and take bets?

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.400
The lowest on the leaderboard:

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.600
chickpeas.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.840
Holy hummus!

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.640
The mightiest free radical
fighter is the fava bean,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.480
with kidneys and pintos
neck and neck for number two.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.160
Lentils were
another big surprise.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.240
I would have guessed
black or red lentils

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.920
to be up there with brown
or green at the bottom.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.040
But check this out.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.960
Green lentils have
about four times

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.920
the antioxidant power
of red ones!

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.520
Next up, how antioxidants may
lower the risk of depression.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.160
According to the latest
from the CDC,

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.360
the rates of all of our top 10 killers
have fallen or stabilized

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.520
except for one...
suicide.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.800
Accumulating evidence indicates
that oxidative free radicals

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.400
may play important roles
in the development

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.960
of various neuropsychiatric disorders
including major depression.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.200
For example, in a study of
nearly 300,000 Canadians,

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.520
greater fruit and vegetable
consumption was associated

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.720
with lower odds of depression,
psychological distress,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.120
self-reported mood and anxiety disorders
and poor perceived mental health.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.680
They conclude that since a
healthy diet comprised of

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.960
a high intake of fruits and vegetables
is rich in anti-oxidants,

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.840
may consequently dampen
the detrimental effects

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.720
of oxidative stress
on mental health.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.200
But that was just
based on asking

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.880
how many fruits and veggies people ate.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.280
If you measure the levels of
carotenoid phytonutrients

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.840
in nearly 2000 people
across the country,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.920
a higher total blood carotenoid
level was associated

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.280
with a lower likelihood of
elevated depressive symptoms,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.000
and there appeared to be a
dose-response relationship,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.920
meaning the higher the levels,
the better people felt.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.600
Lycopene, the red pigment
predominantly found in tomatoes,

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:07.600
but also present in watermelon,
pink grapefruit, guava, papaya,

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.120
is the most powerful antioxidant
among the carotenoid family.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.680
In a test tube it’s about
100 times more effective

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.560
at quenching these free radicals
than vitamin E, for example.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.040
And in a study of about a
thousand older men and women,

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.120
those who ate the
most tomato products

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.680
had about half the
odds of depression.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.360
The researchers conclude that
a tomato-rich diet

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.960
may have a beneficial effect on the
prevention of depressive symptoms.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.200
Higher intake of fruits
and vegetables has been found

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.400
to lead to a lower risk of
developing depression.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.480
But if it’s the antioxidants can’t we
just take an antioxidant pill?

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.440
No, only food sources
of antioxidants

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.520
were protectively associated
with depression.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.200
Not antioxidants from
dietary supplements.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.840
Although plant foods and
food-derived phytochemicals

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.600
have been associated
with health benefits,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.160
antioxidants from dietary
supplements appear to be

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.920
less beneficial and may, in fact,
be detrimental to health.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.160
This may indicate that
the form and delivery

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.800
of the antioxidants
are important.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.600
Alternately, the observed
association may be due

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.120
not to antioxidants at all, but
rather to other dietary factors

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.920
such as folate that also occur in fruits,
vegetables, and plant-rich diets.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.280
In a study of thousands of
middle-aged office workers,

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.920
eating lots of processed food
was found to be a risk factor

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.280
for at least mild to moderate
depression five years later,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.080
whereas a whole food pattern
was found to be protective.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.080
Yes, it could be because of the high content
of antioxidants in fruits and vegetables

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.920
but could also be the folate
in greens and beans,

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.960
as some studies have suggested
an increased risk of depression

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.960
in folks who may not have
been getting enough.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.440
Low folate levels in the blood
are associated with depression,

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.760
but since most of the early
studies were cross-sectional,

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.360
meaning a snapshot
in time,

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.640
we didn’t know if the low
folate led to depression

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.280
or the depression
led to low folate.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.680
Maybe when you have the blues you
don’t want to eat the greens.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.480
But since then a number of
cohort studies were published,

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:09.920
following people over time,

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.280
and a low dietary intake of folate
may indeed be a risk factor

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.720
for severe depression, as much
as a threefold higher risk.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:23.200
Note this is dietary folate intake,
not folic acid supplements,

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.120
so they were actually
eating healthy foods.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.880
If you give people folic acid pills
they don’t seem to work.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.880
This may be because folate is found in
dark green leafy vegetables like spinach,

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.680
whereas folic acid is the
oxidized synthetic compound

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.080
used in food fortification
and dietary supplements

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.320
because it’s
more shelf-stable,

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.440
but may have different effects on
the body as I explored previously.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.760
These kinds of findings
point to the importance

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.320
of antioxidant food sources RATHER
than dietary supplements.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:58.080
But there was an interesting study
giving people high dose vitamin C,

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.240
also known as
ascorbic acid.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:04.080
The vitamin C, but not placebo group,
experienced a decrease

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.560
in depression scores,
and also greater FSI.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:11.120
What is FSI?

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:15.120
FSI evidently stands for
penile-vaginal intercourse,

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.160
an acronym that makes
no sense to me.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.160
But evidently high dose
vitamin C

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.040
improves mood and
intercourse frequency,

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.880
but only in sexual partners that
don’t live with one another.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.120
In the placebo group,
those not living together

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.320
had sex about
once a week,

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.560
and those living together a little higher,
once every five days,

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.920
but no big change
on vitamin C.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:41.840
But those not living
together on vitamin C,

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.080
every other day!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:46.720
The differential effect on
non-cohabitants suggests

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.640
that the mechanism is
not a peripheral one,

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:51.440
meaning outside of the brain,
but a central one—

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.800
some psychological change
which motivates the person

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.240
to venture forth to
have intercourse.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.480
The mild antidepressant
effect they found

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.040
was unrelated to cohabitation
or frequency,

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.160
so it does not appear that the
depression scores improved

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.320
just because of
the improved FSI.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.280
Finally today,

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.000
to stay out of oxidative debt,

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.200
we need to take in more
antioxidants than we use up.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:23.760
The postprandial state is
a pro-oxidant state,

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.480
meaning that after each meal
free radicals are produced

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.320
as our body assimilates the food,

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.480
and so you can't just
have a bowl of berries

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.240
in the morning to
meet our minimum

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:35.440
daily antioxidant needs
and call it a day.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:38.960
Each and every meal
should contain

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.120
high antioxidant foods, which,

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.040
if you remember, means plants.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.480
Antioxidant rich foods originate
from the plant kingdom.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.320
This is due to the
thousands of natural

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.920
antioxidant compounds found
naturally in plant foods.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.840
So, for example,
consuming fruits,

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.600
which are high in
phenolic phytonutrients,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.600
increases the antioxidant
capacity of the blood,

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.800
and when they are
consumed with

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.960
the standard American
diet high fat

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.520
and refined carbohydrate, pro-oxidant,

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.200
and pro-inflammatory’ meals,

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.320
they may help counterbalance
some of the negative effects.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.760
Given the content
and availability

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.520
of fat and sugars in
the Western diet,

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.840
regular consumption of
phenolic-rich foods,

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.840
particularly in
conjunction with meals,

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.200
appears to be a
prudent strategy

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.320
to maintain oxidative
balance and health.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:25.926
And of all fruits,
berries may be the best.

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:27.760
Add a glass of red wine,

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:30.080
which contains berry
phytonutrients from grapes,

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.560
and we can bring down
the level of oxidation,

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.640
but not blunt it completely.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.080
So the meal needs
even more plants.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:41.680
In this study, they gave people
standard breakfast items,

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.360
resulting in lots of oxidized
cholesterol in their blood stream

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.000
1,2,3,4,5,6 hours after the meal.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.240
But all it took was
a cup of strawberries

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.640
with that same breakfast to
at least keep the meal

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.360
from contributing to
further oxidation.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.840
Note though, without
the strawberries,

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.080
look where we'd
be at lunchtime.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.053
Let's say we ate a standard
American diet at 6 am.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.120
If we didn’t eat that cup of
strawberries with breakfast,

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.480
by the time lunch rolls
around we'd already be

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.680
starting out in a
hyper-oxidized state

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:18.480
and could just
make things worse.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.640
Since western eating
patterns include

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.880
eating multiple meals a day,
including snacks,

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:26.800
one can only speculate on the
level of biological unrest.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.360
But, at least if we had
some berries for breakfast

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:33.200
we'd be starting out
at baseline for lunch.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.800
This acute protection
is likely due

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:39.040
to the antioxidant effects of
the strawberry phytonutrients.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.160
Even better than baseline,
how about our meal

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.120
actually improving our
antioxidant status?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.960
Here's measuring the
antioxidant level

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.280
of one's bloodstream
after a crappy meal.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:52.960
It drops, using up our
antioxidant stores,

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.800
but eat a big bunch of
red grapes with the meal

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.680
and the antioxidant level of
our bloodstream goes up,

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.920
such that our body
is in a positive

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:04.480
antioxidant balance
for a few hours.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:07.360
Same thing after
enough blueberries.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:11.520
And imagine if in these ensuing
hours between our next meal

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.080
we were sipping green
tea or hibiscus?

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.400
We'd have this nice antioxidant
surplus all day long.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:22.160
What, according to the researchers,
are the practical implications?

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.120
These data provide an
interesting perspective

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.760
for advising individuals
on food choices

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:29.600
when consuming a moderate to&nbsp;

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:33.814
high fat meal is unavoidable.
76&nbsp;

00:11:33.814 --> 00:11:35.040
00:03:41,3 --&gt; 00:03:43,04
Unavoidable?!

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:40.000
So, if we're like locked in a
fast food joint or something?

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.080
Well, then they suggest
chasing whatever

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.600
you’re forced to eat
with some berries.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.040
Reminds me of those&nbsp;

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.534
studies on smokers
81&nbsp;

00:11:46.534 --> 00:11:48.240
00:03:54,4 --&gt; 00:03:58,11
I talked about, suggesting&nbsp;

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:48.880
those who smoke

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.400
should eat lots of
kale and broccoli

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.680
to reduce the oxidative
damage to their DNA.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:57.440
Or...they could
just not smoke.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.920
In a single day,
the systemic stress

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.800
of all the fat in your
blood and redox imbalance

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.080
(being in a mild pro-oxidant
state after meals)

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.520
may seem trivial.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.760
Over time, however,
these daily insults

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:12.480
can lead to complicated
atherosclerosis,

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.440
contributing to hundreds of
thousands of deaths a year.

